            <td height="5" width="47%"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>Pro-Palestinian 
              criticism of Palestinians and their supporters</b></font></td>
            <td height="5" colspan="2"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="5" width="45%"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>Pro-Israeli 
              criticism of Israelis and their supporters </b></font></td>
          </tr>

          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="5" colspan="3"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="5" colspan="4"> 
              <hr size="1">
            </td>
          </tr>

          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="5" colspan="3"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="5" width="47%"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="5" colspan="2"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="5" width="45%"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="449" colspan="3"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="449" width="47%"> 
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">1) Failure 
                of Palestinian leaders to articulate a specific mission and a 
                clear vision for their struggle. As much as they have been successful 
                in mobilizing public world opinion to their side, they still have 
                not been able to do it to the successful extent that the South 
                Africans were able to do against Apartheid. </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 2) Absence 
                of a long-term non-violent strategy that unites all Palestinians 
                in their struggle against the occupation. The Palestinian cause 
                can be pushed quite far if the Palestinian leadership invested 
                some of its effort in developing creative non-violent resistance 
                effort against which the IDF would be totally powerless.</font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 3) Failure 
                of Arabs and Muslims to offer the Palestinians strong and consistent 
                backing beyond the usual empty rhetoric: e.g., money, economic 
                sanctions against the United States (as in passing legislation 
                that would block Arab companies from doing business with US companies 
                and passing them over for European companies).</font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 4) Cynical 
                exploitation of the Palestinian struggle by Arab dictators primarily 
                concerned with detracting attention from their miserable regimes. 
                </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 5) Lack of 
                respect for democratic principles and the rule of law by the Palestinian 
                Authority, and the attendant corruption. </font>
            </p></td>
            <td height="449" colspan="2"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="449" width="45%"> 
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">1) Israelis 
                should work much harder to empathize with the predicament of the 
                Palestinians and translate that empathy into action. </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 2) I have 
                lots of criticism for the whole settlement movement. </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 3) I don't 
                agree with the basic format of the Israeli government - I believe 
                in the American system, the two-party, representative democratic 
                system - I think that it fosters moderation. The current parliamentary 
                system with multiple parties fosters too much catering to extreme 
                elements. </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 4) I yearn 
                for greater Jewish religious diversity in Israel - there is too 
                much polarization between the ultra-Orthodox and the secular - 
                I think that the secular position is attractive as a response 
                to the ultra-Orthodox. </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 5) I wish 
                that more visionary leaders were at hand to lead the way to a 
                firm, just peace. </font>
            </p></td>
          </tr>
	
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="5" colspan="3"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="5" width="47%"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="5" colspan="2"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
            <td height="5" width="45%"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"></font></td>
